Clean-room statement
====================

remacs re-implements the observable behavior of a subset of GNU Emacs.

- No GNU Emacs source code, C or Lisp, has been read or copied in the
  making of this program.
- No GNU Emacs docstrings are quoted.
- The interfaces used are limited to: function names, their argument
  conventions, and behavior as publicly documented or as observed by
  running GNU Emacs as an unmodified black box.
- GNU Emacs binaries are used only as a test oracle: test programs are
  executed against both remacs and GNU Emacs, and their outputs are
  compared. The oracle's output is not stored in this repository.

remacs is an independent work and is not affiliated with or endorsed by
the GNU Project or the Free Software Foundation.
